From c80fe91a743966769b7836c49b5c04af9da95e3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:54:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] feat(harmony): drop daemon connections while the app is
 in the background

HarmonyOS freezes a backgrounded app within seconds and its sockets go
silent without closing. A daemon that still sees the phone connected, and
recently used, hands it an in-app alert nobody receives, and pushes nothing,
until the relay lease runs out. The HarmonyOS build now suspends every
client when the app leaves the foreground, so the daemon pushes from the
first moment, and resumes them when it returns.

DaemonClient gains suspend() and resume(): the connection drops through the
same path a failed liveness check takes, subscriptions and state survive,
and nothing reconnects until resume(), which reconnects at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
